## Orchestrator visual and keyboard verification

Result: all performed checks passed in the mock-only local production preview. Full matrix and artifacts are in [visual-verification.md](visual-verification.md), with measurements and screenshots under `visual/`.

Coverage included Student, TA, and Coordinator headers at 320/640/1280 CSS px; nine viewport measurements showed no horizontal overflow, overlap, clipping, or emoji, with controls at least 42 px high and role-specific links/active state. TA/Coordinator account forms were checked across all three widths; Student wrong-password feedback was checked at all three widths. Keyboard focus showed a visible 3 px outline; hover styling was visible. Wrong-password error placement, ARIA association, focus, correction behavior, and absence of Retry were inspected, along with session Sign in feedback. Loading, empty, populated, inbox failure, mark-read failure, and direct reload retained the header.

Limit: all browser network responses were synthetic mock fixtures; this is not live backend/cloud verification. Manager retry and protected logout were verified by integration tests, not browser actions. One read-only DOM value-attribute equality probe was inconclusive; screenshot evidence showed the edited non-secret email remained visible. No production corrections followed visual inspection.

